# Skills that chezmoi used to manage in ~/.claude/skills and no longer does.
#
# `chezmoi apply` never deletes a file just because the source stopped managing
# it, so deleting a skill from private_dot_claude/skills/ leaves the applied copy
# behind on every machine that had already applied it. That is not cosmetic. Three
# of the names below (prototype, research, grill-me) were dropped from this repo
# precisely so they could be served from Matt Pocock's upstream instead, and the
# stale directory sitting at the target path is what the link script refuses to
# clobber -- so the orphan does not merely linger, it blocks its own replacement.
# The other three are the review1st/review3rd rename and a deletion; leaving those
# behind means the old and new names are both live skills with the same content,
# and an agent picking between them can pick the stale one.
#
# Why every entry is guarded on not-a-symlink. An unguarded `.chezmoiremove` entry
# is a booby trap for exactly the three link-script names: the first apply removes
# the stale directory and the script links the replacement, but the entry is still
# there on the *next* apply, which deletes the symlink -- and
# run_onchange_after_link-mp-skills.sh will not re-run to restore it, because its
# hash has not changed. The skill silently disappears and stays gone. Verified,
# not theorised. lstat (not stat -- stat follows the link and reports "dir") tells
# the two cases apart, so the rule each line encodes is "remove a real directory
# that nothing manages any more; never touch a symlink someone installed".
#
# Removal is processed before run_onchange_after_* scripts, so a machine that has
# not synced since these were deleted clears the orphan and links the replacement
# in a single `chezmoi apply` -- no second pass, no manual rm.
#
# Gated on .claudecfg for the same reason the clone and the link script are: in a
# container devlaunch bind-mounts the *host's* ~/.claude read-write, and removing
# through that mount would delete the host's real skills.
#
# These lines are a migration, not a permanent fixture. Once every machine has
# synced past this commit they are all no-ops and can be dropped.
{{ if .claudecfg -}}
{{   range list
       ".claude/skills/prototype"
       ".claude/skills/research"
       ".claude/skills/grill-me"
       ".claude/skills/review1st"
       ".claude/skills/review3rd"
       ".claude/skills/ubiquitous-language" -}}
{{     $rel := . -}}
{{     with lstat (joinPath $.chezmoi.homeDir $rel) -}}
{{       if ne .type "symlink" }}{{ $rel }}
{{       end -}}
{{     end -}}
{{   end -}}
{{ end -}}
